# Keep the production image lean + correct — ship the live backend, the pages it serves and what its routes read.
# W1128 - a comment is a line of its own: Docker reads "#" as a comment only at the start of a line, so a pattern
# with a comment after it matched nothing (apps/, data/ and integration_tests/ were never left out).
.git
.github
_archive/
# the pages are built inside the image (its pages stage), so their sources are in the build context; what a local
# install or build left behind is not
**/node_modules/
apps/workstation-superapp/dist/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
# runtime data — mounted as a volume / DATA_DIR in production
data/
*.log
.env
.env.*
# tests run in CI, not shipped in the runtime image
integration_tests/
.claude/
# audit records; no route reads them
docs/fidelity_runs/
# W1128 (FU-1156) - every private folder (agentic_core/privacy_exposure.py PRIVATE_FOLDERS, W731) stays out of the
# build context, whatever a working copy holds
inputs/Law/
inputs/Employment/
knowledge/Employment/
knowledge/Science/RM_CV_Science_Versions/
knowledge/Law/EmploymentTribunal/evidence/
products/Law/VSB-SIG-LAW-OMNIOCTO-19.0/
products/Employment/VSB-SIG-EMP-PENTA-3.0/
products/Science/VSB-SIG-SCI-OMNIA-18.0/
outputs/education/sats_2026/
